---
// /what-we-treat/mental-health/personality-disorders/: What-We-Treat-Content-Briefs.md §M. Sources in
// docs/content/what-we-treat-sources-mental.md. Rotation: Reviews only. Reviewed by Dana.
import ServicePage from '../../../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import NextSteps from '../../../components/NextSteps.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import { WWT, CATEGORIES, MENTAL_PAGES } from '../../../data/treat.js';
import { conditionAbout } from '../../../lib/programSchema.js';

const path = '/what-we-treat/mental-health/personality-disorders/';

const signs = [
  'Relationships keep following the same painful pattern',
  'Emotions hit fast and hard, and using takes the edge off',
  'Feedback feels like an attack, even when it isn’t meant as one',
  'You’ve tried treatment before and felt misunderstood',
];

const treating = [
  { icon: 'users', title: 'A relational lens', text: 'We look at the relationships, family systems and learned patterns around you, not just at a diagnosis. People are shaped by their experiences, and can create something different.' },
  { icon: 'message', title: 'Carefrontation in group', text: 'Honest feedback, given with care and without shame. You practice hearing hard things without shutting down, and saying them without attacking.' },
  { icon: 'heart', title: 'A strong therapeutic relationship', text: 'Our lead therapist’s work centers on the therapeutic alliance and connection as drivers of lasting change. That relationship is where new patterns get practiced first.' },
  { icon: 'refresh', title: 'Patterns in real time', text: 'You go home every day. The conflict at home or at work comes back to group, where we slow it down and look at what happened.' },
];

const approaches = [
  { name: 'DBT', text: 'Builds skills for emotional regulation, distress tolerance and relationships: the core of how we work with intense emotions.' },
  { name: 'Internal Family Systems (IFS)', text: 'Helps you understand the different parts of yourself, including the protective ones that react before you can think.' },
  { name: 'Psychodynamic therapy', text: 'Looks at how early experiences and relationships formed the patterns you live within today.' },
  { name: 'Family systems work', text: 'Explores the roles and patterns in your family that may keep the cycle going, with your consent.' },
  { name: 'CBT', text: 'Works on the thoughts and beliefs that drive reactions and substance use.' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Do you treat borderline personality disorder?', a: 'Personality disorders are among the conditions we see most often alongside substance use. Your pre-screening and intake assessment help us understand your specific needs and recommend the right level of care. <a href="/admissions/">Start with admissions</a>.' },
  { q: 'Will I be treated as a label?', a: 'No. We approach people with curiosity rather than judgment. Instead of asking what’s wrong with you, we want to understand what happened to you and what patterns you’ve been living within.' },
  { q: 'Is group therapy right for me if relationships are hard?', a: 'Group is often where the most useful work happens. The same facilitator leads the whole session, and our carefrontation culture teaches honest feedback without shame, so you can practice new ways of relating with support.' },
  { q: 'Do you treat personality disorders without substance use?', a: 'Our programs are built for people living with substance use and co-occurring mental health conditions together. If that isn’t your situation, call us anyway and we’ll help you find the right kind of care.' },
  { q: 'Which program should I start in?', a: 'Our Clinical Director reviews your pre-screening and recommends a level of care using ASAM criteria and clinical judgment. <a href="/programs/">Compare PHP, IOP and OP</a>.' },
];
---
<ServicePage
  path={path}
  metaTitle="Personality Disorder Treatment in West Palm Beach | Sunview"
  description="Personality disorders treated alongside substance use in West Palm Beach. DBT, IFS and psychodynamic work in outpatient PHP, IOP and OP."
  crumbs={[WWT, { name: CATEGORIES.mental.name, href: CATEGORIES.mental.href }, { name: 'Personality Disorders', href: path }]}
  h1="Personality Disorder and Addiction Treatment in West Palm Beach"
  subheading="Understanding the patterns, not labeling the person."
  lead="Personality disorders treated alongside substance use in outpatient PHP, IOP and OP, with DBT, IFS and relational work that helps you understand the patterns you live within, and change them."
  faqTitle="Frequently Asked Questions About Personality Disorder Treatment"
  faqs={faqs}
  reviews
  about={conditionAbout('Personality disorders')}
>
  {/* The cycle */}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">The cycle</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">How Personality Disorders and Substance Use Feed Each Other</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Old patterns, new consequences</p>
        <div class="prose-sv mt-6">
          <p>At Sunview, personality disorders are treated as part of <a href="/what-we-treat/dual-diagnosis/">dual diagnosis treatment</a>, alongside substance use, within our Partial Hospitalization, Intensive Outpatient and Outpatient programs. They are among the presentations we see most often in people who come to us for addiction treatment.</p>
          <p>Long-standing patterns in how you feel, react and relate to others can make life feel unstable. Substances often become a way to manage intense emotions or painful relationships. Then using adds its own conflict and fallout, and the patterns get stronger.</p>
          <p>We don’t believe anyone is born “bad” or destined to struggle. People are shaped by their experiences, relationships and environments. Understanding that is where change starts.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {/* REVIEW 8.5: plain-language passage pending Elizabeth review */}
      <aside class="card self-start !p-7">
        <h3 class="text-xl">Signs the two may be connected</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          {signs.map((s) => <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check" class="mt-1 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-teal" />{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Treating it at Sunview */}
  <section class="section bg-mist">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-5xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">At Sunview</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Treating Personality Disorders Alongside Addiction at Sunview</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Compassion without avoiding accountability</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        {treating.map((t) => (
          <div class="card">
            <Icon name={t.icon} class="h-7 w-7 text-teal" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl">{t.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2">{t.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Therapies */}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Therapy</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Therapy Approaches We Use</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Skills and insight, practiced in relationship</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg">DBT gives you tools for the moment. Deeper work helps you see why the moments happen. Both get practiced with real people: your therapist and your group.</p>
        <a href="/therapies/" class="btn-teal mt-8">How therapy works at Sunview <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
      <dl class="divide-y divide-line self-start rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-line">
        {approaches.map((a) => (
          <div class="grid gap-1 p-6 sm:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] sm:gap-6">
            <dt class="font-extrabold">{a.name}</dt>
            <dd>{a.text}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Psychiatry */}
  <section class="section bg-mist">
    <div class="container-x grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Medication</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Psychiatric Care and Medication</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">One part of the work, integrated into your program</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg">Psychiatric evaluation and medication management are part of every program through our partner, Telemed Clinix. Your provider looks at what you already take and adjusts only when it’s clinically indicated, as part of the same plan your therapist is working from.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg">Medication can support stability. The relational and therapeutic work is where lasting change happens. You can keep the same provider after you finish.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card !p-8">
        <Icon name="pill" class="h-8 w-8 text-teal" />
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl">What psychiatric care includes</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal" />Evaluation and review of your current medications</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal" />Appointments scheduled for you, on site</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal" />The same provider after discharge, if you want</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/programs/psychiatry-medication-management/" class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-teal underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-teal-light">Psychiatric care and medication management <Icon name="arrow" class="h-4 w-4" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextSteps
    class="section"
    title="Which Level of Care Fits"
    subtitle="Our Clinical Director helps you decide"
    level={`<p>Many people start in the <a href="/programs/php/">Partial Hospitalization Program</a>, where daily group work gives patterns room to show up and change. The <a href="/programs/iop/">Intensive Outpatient Program</a>, day or evening, fits when you need depth and have to keep working. The <a href="/programs/outpatient/">Outpatient Program</a> keeps support in place as new patterns settle in.</p>`}
    related={[
      { label: 'Co-occurring mental health treatment', href: CATEGORIES.mental.href },
      ...MENTAL_PAGES.filter((p) => p.href !== path).map((p) => ({ label: p.label, href: p.href })),
      { label: 'Dual diagnosis treatment', href: CATEGORIES.dual.href },
      { label: 'Substance use disorder treatment', href: CATEGORIES.substance.href },
    ]}
  />
</ServicePage>
